# Big Mart Sales Prediction

## Project Overview

This project predicts the sales of products in Big Mart stores using Linear Regression.
It uses a dataset taken from Kaggle and applies machine learning techniques to estimate sales based on product and store details.

---

## Objective

The main objective of this project is to predict **Item Outlet Sales** and understand how different features affect sales.
It also demonstrates the use of Linear Regression in a real-world problem.

---

## Dataset

The dataset used in this project is obtained from Kaggle.
It contains information about products and outlets such as:

* Item Weight
* Item Visibility
* Item MRP
* Outlet Establishment Year
* Item Type
* Outlet Size
* Outlet Location Type
* Outlet Type

**Target Variable:**

* Item_Outlet_Sales

---

## Model Used

This project uses **Linear Regression**, a supervised machine learning algorithm used to predict continuous values.
It finds a relationship between input features and the target variable (sales).

---

## Methodology

* Data cleaning and preprocessing
* Handling missing values
* Converting categorical data into numerical form
* Splitting data into training and testing sets
* Training the Linear Regression model
* Making predictions

---

## Deployment

The model is deployed using Streamlit to create a simple user interface where users can input values and get predicted sales.

---

## Conclusion

This project shows how Linear Regression can be used to solve real-world prediction problems.
It covers the complete process from data preprocessing to deployment.

---

